- `targetDate`: A JavaScript Date object representing the target date and time for the countdown.
- `format`: A string specifying the format in which the countdown should be displayed (e.g., "dd:hh:mm:ss").
- `onTick`: A callback function that should be called on each tick of the countdown timer.
- `onFinish`: A callback function that should be called when the countdown reaches zero.

The countdown timer should update its display every second and should be customizable using CSS.

Your task is to implement the `countdownTimer` jQuery plugin and provide an example of its usage.

### Solution:
```javascript
// jQuery plugin definition
(function($) {
  $.fn.countdownTimer = function(options) {
    // Default options
    var settings = $.extend({
      targetDate: new Date(),
      format: "dd:hh:mm:ss",
      onTick: function() {},
      onFinish: function() {}
    }, options);

    // Iterate over the matched elements
    return this.each(function() {
      var $this = $(this);

      // Update countdown display
      function updateCountdown() {
        var now = new Date().getTime();
        var distance = settings.targetDate.getTime() - now;

        if (distance <= 0) {
          clearInterval(timerInterval);
          settings.onFinish();
        } else {
          var days = Math.floor(distance / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24));
          var hours = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24)) / (1000 * 60 * 60));
          var minutes = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60 * 60)) / (1000 * 60));
          var seconds = Math.floor((distance % (1000 * 60)) / 1000);

          var formattedTime = settings.format
            .replace("dd", days)
            .replace("hh", hours)
            .replace("mm", minutes)
            .replace("ss", seconds);

          $this.text(formattedTime);
          settings.onTick();
        }
      }

      // Initial call to update countdown
      updateCountdown();

      // Update countdown every second
      var timerInterval = setInterval(updateCountdown, 1000);
    });
  };
})(jQuery);

// Example usage
$(document).ready(function() {
  $("#countdown").countdownTimer({
    targetDate: new Date("2023-01-01T00:00:00"),
    format: "dd days, hh hours, mm minutes, ss seconds",
    onTick: function() {
      console.log("Tick");
    },
    onFinish: function() {
      console.log("Countdown finished");
    }
  });
});
```

In this solution, we define a jQuery plugin called `countdownTimer` that accepts a configuration object with various options for customizing the countdown timer. The plugin updates the countdown display every second and triggers the specified callback functions on each tick and when the countdown finishes. The example usage demonstrates how to initialize the countdown timer on an element with the ID `countdown` and customize its behavior and appearance.

