### Solution:
```rust
/// Enum representing known regions
enum Region {
    // Define the known regions
    Asia,
    Europe,
    NorthAmerica,
    SouthAmerica,
    Africa,
    Oceania,
}

impl Region {
    /// Attempt to create a region from a string
    fn from_str(s: &str) -> Option<Region> {
        match s {
            "asia" => Some(Region::Asia),
            "eu" | "europe" => Some(Region::Europe),
            "na" | "northamerica" => Some(Region::NorthAmerica),
            "sa" | "southamerica" => Some(Region::SouthAmerica),
            "africa" => Some(Region::Africa),
            "oceania" => Some(Region::Oceania),
            _ => None,
        }
    }

    /// Get the name of the region
    fn name(&self) -> &str {
        match self {
            Region::Asia => "Asia",
            Region::Europe => "Europe",
            Region::NorthAmerica => "North America",
            Region::SouthAmerica => "South America",
            Region::Africa => "Africa",
            Region::Oceania => "Oceania",
        }
    }
}

/// Translate a hostname into a region name by finding the first part of
/// the domain name that matches a known region.
fn region_name_from_host(host: &str) -> Option<String> {
    host.split('.')
        .filter_map(|part| Region::from_str(part).ok())
        .map(|region| region.name().into())
        .next()
}

fn main() {
    let hostname = "eu.example.com";
    match region_name_from_host(hostname) {
        Some(region) => println!("The region for {} is {}", hostname, region),
        None => println!("No region found for {}", hostname),
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `Region` enum is defined to represent the known regions. The `from_str` method attempts to create a region from a string, and the `name` method returns the name of the region. The `region_name_from_host` function is completed to split the hostname, filter and map the parts to regions, and return the first result as an optional region name. Finally, in the `main` function, an example usage of `region_name_from_host` is demonstrated.

