        <img src="https://img.shields.io/crates/d/fp-rs.svg?style=flat-square" alt="Download" />
      </a>
    </div>
    "#;

    if let Some((version, downloads)) = parseBadges(html) {
        println!("Version: {}, Downloads: {}", version, downloads);
    } else {
        println!("Unable to parse badges");
    }
}
```
The `parseBadges` function uses regular expressions to extract the version number and download count from the input HTML. It first matches the version number using the `img_regex` and then matches the download count using the `a_regex`. If both matches are successful, it returns a `Some` containing the extracted version number and download count. Otherwise, it returns `None`.

### Problem:
You are working on a large C++ project that involves the simulation of fluid dynamics using the Newtonian Euler equations. The codebase contains several namespaces and tags related to various properties of the fluid. The IWYU (Include What You Use) pragma is used to enforce that certain tags should not be forward declared. 

Your task is to write a function that processes a given list of IWYU pragmas and identifies the tags that should not be forward declared. 

Write a function `findForbiddenTags` that takes a list of IWYU pragmas as input and returns a list of tags that should not be forward declared. The IWYU pragma format is as follows:
```
// IWYU pragma: no_forward_declare Namespace::Tags::Tag
```
The function should return a list of unique tags that appear in the input list of IWYU pragmas.

Function Signature: 
```cpp
std::vector<std::string> findForbiddenTags(const std::vector<std::string>& iwyuPragmas);
```

Example:
```cpp
std::vector<std::string> iwyuPragmas = {
    "// IWYU pragma: no_forward_declare NewtonianEuler::Tags::Pressure",
    "// IWYU pragma: no_forward_declare NewtonianEuler::Tags::SpecificInternalEnergy",
    "// IWYU pragma: no_forward_declare NewtonianEuler::Tags::Velocity"
};

std::vector<std::string> forbiddenTags = findForbiddenTags(iwyuPragmas);
// forbiddenTags should be {"NewtonianEuler::Tags::Pressure", "NewtonianEuler::Tags::SpecificInternalEnergy", "NewtonianEuler::Tags::Velocity"}
```

### Solution:
```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <unordered_set>

std::vector<std::string> findForbiddenTags(const std::vector<std::string>& iwyuPragmas) {
    std::unordered_set<std::string> forbiddenTagsSet;
    for (const std::string& pragma : iwyuPragmas) {
        size_t startPos = pragma.find("no_forward_declare");
        if (startPos != std::string::npos) {
            size_t tagStartPos = pragma.find("::", startPos);
            if (tagStartPos != std::string::npos) {
                size_t tagEndPos = pragma.find(" ", tagStartPos);
                if (tagEndPos != std::string::npos) {
                    std::string tag = pragma.substr(tagStartPos, tagEndPos - tagStartPos);
                    forbiddenTagsSet.insert(tag);
                }
            }
        }
    }
    return std::vector<std::string>(forbiddenTagsSet.begin(), forbiddenTagsSet.end());
}
```

