fn get_enabled_features(feature_names: Vec<&str>, config: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut enabled_features = Vec::new();
    for line in config.lines() {
        for feature in &feature_names {
            if line.contains(&format!("feature = \"{}\"", feature)) {
                let feature_name = line.trim().split('"').nth(1).unwrap().to_string();
                enabled_features.push(feature_name);
            }
        }
    }
    enabled_features
}
```

The `get_enabled_features` function iterates through each line in the configuration and checks if it contains the feature name. If a match is found, it extracts the feature name and adds it to the list of enabled features. The function then returns the list of enabled features based on the configuration.

