  if (condition) {
    return true;
  }
}
```
The function call `isValidCodeSnippet(code)` should return false, as the closing curly brace `}` is followed by the `if` statement on the same line.

### Solution:
```javascript
function isValidCodeSnippet(code) {
  const lines = code.split('\n');
  let openingBraceCount = 0;
  let closingBraceCount = 0;

  for (let line of lines) {
    line = line.trim();
    if (line.includes('{')) {
      openingBraceCount++;
      if (!line.includes('}')) {
        return false;
      }
    }
    if (line.includes('}')) {
      closingBraceCount++;
      if (line.indexOf('}') !== line.length - 1) {
        return false;
      }
    }
  }

  return openingBraceCount > 0 && openingBraceCount === closingBraceCount;
}
```

The `isValidCodeSnippet` function splits the input code into lines and iterates through each line to count the occurrences of opening and closing curly braces. It checks if the opening and closing braces are present on the same line and if the closing brace is not followed by any other characters. If the counts match and the conditions are met, the function returns true; otherwise, it returns false.

