### Problem:
You are given a code snippet that appears to be part of a Rust program. The snippet contains a macro invocation `benches!` with several comma-separated pairs of identifiers and numbers. Your task is to write a program that parses this input and organizes it into a data structure for further processing.

Write a Rust program that reads the input from the code snippet and constructs a data structure to store the pairs of identifiers and numbers. The program should then provide functionality to perform the following operations:
1. Retrieve the number associated with a given identifier.
2. Retrieve the identifier associated with a given number.
3. Find the maximum number and its associated identifier.
4. Find the minimum number and its associated identifier.

Your program should handle the case where there are multiple identifiers with the same number, and it should return any one of the matching identifiers for the given number.

### Solution:
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;

struct Benchmarks {
    data: HashMap<String, u32>,
}

impl Benchmarks {
    fn new() -> Benchmarks {
        Benchmarks {
            data: HashMap::new(),
        }
    }

    fn add_benchmark(&mut self, identifier: &str, number: u32) {
        self.data.insert(identifier.to_string(), number);
    }

    fn get_number(&self, identifier: &str) -> Option<u32> {
        self.data.get(identifier).cloned()
    }

    fn get_identifier(&self, number: u32) -> Option<&String> {
        self.data.iter().find(|&(_, &v)| v == number).map(|(k, _)| k)
    }

    fn max_number(&self) -> Option<(&String, &u32)> {
        self.data.iter().max_by_key(|&(_, v)| v)
    }

    fn min_number(&self) -> Option<(&String, &u32)> {
        self.data.iter().min_by_key(|&(_, v)| v)
    }
}

fn main() {
    let mut benchmarks = Benchmarks::new();

    benchmarks.add_benchmark("p00024", 24);
    benchmarks.add_benchmark("p00053", 53);
    benchmarks.add_benchmark("p00100", 100);
    benchmarks.add_benchmark("p01000", 1000);
    benchmarks.add_benchmark("p10000", 10000);

    println!("Number for p00100: {:?}", benchmarks.get_number("p00100"));
    println!("Identifier for number 1000: {:?}", benchmarks.get_identifier(1000).unwrap());
    println!("Max number and identifier: {:?}", benchmarks.max_number().unwrap());
    println!("Min number and identifier: {:?}", benchmarks.min_number().unwrap());
}
```

