### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a function that takes an object as input and returns a new object with the keys and values reversed. If the input object has nested objects, the function should also reverse the keys and values of the nested objects. If the input object has arrays as values, the function should reverse the elements of those arrays.

For example, given the following input:
```javascript
const input = {
  name: "John",
  age: 30,
  address: {
    city: "New York",
    country: "USA"
  },
  hobbies: ["reading", "hiking"]
};
```
The function should return:
```javascript
{
  John: "name",
  30: "age",
  address: {
    New York: "city",
    USA: "country"
  },
  hobbies: ["gnidaer", "gnikih"]
}
```

Your task is to implement the function `reverseKeysAndValues(input)`.

### Solution:
```javascript
function reverseKeysAndValues(input) {
  if (typeof input !== 'object' || input === null) {
    return input;
  }

  if (Array.isArray(input)) {
    return input.map(reverseKeysAndValues);
  }

  const result = {};
  for (const key in input) {
    if (typeof input[key] === 'object' && !Array.isArray(input[key])) {
      result[input[key]] = reverseKeysAndValues(key);
    } else if (Array.isArray(input[key])) {
      result[key] = input[key].map((item) => {
        return typeof item === 'object' ? reverseKeysAndValues(item) : item.toString().split('').reverse().join('');
      });
    } else {
      result[input[key]] = key;
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

